  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14269732/assets/f0cef488e0c3940f27ccbf13d2df314fd50e51759f54f6ff92113aa58c7e990d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, $b≈${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\n{b}^{2}={a}^{2}+{c}^{2}-2ac\\operatorname{cos}⁡A.\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm∠A={140}^{∘},\\,a=15,\\,c=7.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2} & ={15}^{2}+{7}^{2}-2(15)(7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{140}^{∘} \\\\  & =225+49-210\\operatorname{cos}⁡{140}^{∘} \\\\  & =274-210(-0.766\\,04…) \\\\  & =274+160.869\\,33 \\\\  & =434.869\\,33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\nb=\\sqrt{434.869\\,33}≈21\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
